# Copy to `.env`. Everything here is EXPO_PUBLIC_*, which means it is INLINED
# INTO THE JS BUNDLE at build time and recoverable from the installed app
# package. Nothing secret belongs in this file.

# Flashnet Orchestra — cross-chain swaps.
#
# MUST be a CLIENT key (fnp_…). Orchestra issues two kinds:
#
#   fnp_…  client key — public, scope-gated, meant to be embedded. Use this.
#   fn_…   server key — secret, FULL account access. Flashnet's own integration
#          guide says "never embed it in mobile or browser apps", and an
#          EXPO_PUBLIC_ value is embedded by definition.
#
# Get one from the Orchestra dashboard. `keyKind()` reports which sort is
# configured; a server key still WORKS, which is what makes it dangerous.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FLASHNET_API_KEY=fnp_replace_me

# Only needed for an ORIGIN-GATED client key — those answer 403
# `origin_required` on /quote and /submit until an Origin header is present.
# React Native's fetch is not a browser and sends none of its own. Any value is
# accepted unless the key has an allowlist, in which case use a registered one.
# Leave unset for a key without that restriction.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FLASHNET_ORIGIN=run.mercury.wallet

# NOTE on reading order status: a client key alone gets 403 `read_token_required`
# from /status. The per-order `readToken` comes back in the /quote response and
# is sent as a `?readToken=` QUERY PARAM alongside the key — not as a header,
# and not in place of it. The app persists it with each swap; see
# `Quote.readToken` in src/bridge/flashnet.ts.

# The hub. Without it the Graph read path (activity, token discovery) returns
# nothing, and incoming-payment notifications have no data source.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RELAYER_URL=

# Optional RPC overrides — the public defaults are rate-limited.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BTC_ESPLORA_MAINNET=
